or patients living with ALS. The drug missed its primary efficacy endpoint, and we’re not advancing the program in ALS.\n\nWhen a drug doesn’t work, the temptation is to look away. We’re going to do the opposite. The trial taught us more than a successful one might have, and we want to share what we learned.\n\nOur first generation discovery engine, CONVERGE 1.0, nominated a drug target called PIKfyve. Our team took it through years of preclinical work, Phase 1 healthy-volunteer studies, and a Phase 1b study in ALS patients. The drug had clear biological activity, including in the brain and the two cell types most central to ALS, neurons and astrocytes. But the patients did not get better. Inside the gap between those two facts, we learned things about the disease and our platform that change how we build the next iteration.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVRG-50635 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents - Synapse (https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/e8eb7239d59844068928864adb4e46cd)\nciteturn198search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Drug Highest Phase Discontinued Phase 1 ... A Phase 1 Study of the Safety, Tolerability, and Pharmacokinetics of VRG50635 in Healthy Volunteers\n\nLast update 22 Aug 2026\n\n# VRG-50635\n\n## Overview\n\n### Basic Info\n\nDrug Type Small molecule drug\nSynonyms VRG50635, VRG635\nTargetPIKFYVE\nAction inhibitors\nMechanism PIKFYVE inhibitors(phosphoinositide kinase, FYVE-type zinc finger containing inhibitors)\nTherapeutic AreasNervous System DiseasesEndocrinology and Metabolic DiseaseOther Diseases\nActive Indication-\nInactive IndicationAmyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis\n\nOriginator OrganizationImage: Verge Analytics, Inc.Verge Analytics, Inc.\nActive Organization-\nInactive OrganizationImage: Verge Analytics, Inc.Verge Analytics, Inc.\nLicense OrganizationImage: Grupo Ferrer Internacional SAGrupo Ferrer Internacional SAImage: Verge Analytics, Inc.Verge Analytics, Inc.\nDrug Highest Phase Discontinued Phase 1\nFirst Approval Date-\nRegulation-\n\n### Related\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNeuvivo appoints Michael McGrath MD, PhD as Chief Executive Officer (https://www.prweb.com/releases/neuvivo-appoints-michael-mcgrath-md-phd-as-chief-executive-officer-302939355.html)\nciteturn198search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; 13, 2026 /PRNewswire-PRWeb/ -- Neuvivo Inc., a late-stage biopharmaceutical company specializing in immunological treatments for neurodegenerative diseases, today announces it has appointed Mike McGrath MD, PhD. as permanent CEO. ... He has led Neuvivo to the threshold of a pivotal Phase 3 trial of NP001, a novel approach designed to restore balance to the innate immune system in ALS - John Curnutte, MD, PhD (Neuvivo Board Member)\n\n# Neuvivo appoints Michael McGrath MD, PhD as Chief Executive Officer\n\n## News provided by\n\nNeuvivo Inc.\n\nNov 13, 2026, 20:00 ET\n\nAppointment follows 12-month interim tenure of scientific, regulatory and commercial achievements for Phase 3 trial preparation in ALS\n\nPALO ALTO, Calif., Nov. 13, 2026 /PRNewswire-PRWeb/ -- Neuvivo Inc., a late-stage biopharmaceutical company specializing in immunological treatments for neurodegenerative diseases, today announces it has appointed Mike McGrath MD, PhD. as permanent CEO.\n\nThe permanent appointment results from what Neuvivo has been able to achieve in Mike's 12-month tenure as interim CEO of Neuvivo, following his appointment by the Neuvivo Board of Directors in October 2025.\n\nHe has led Neuvivo to the threshold of a pivotal Phase 3 trial of NP001, a novel approach designed to restore balance to the innate immune system in ALS - John Curnutte, MD, PhD (Neuvivo Board Member)\n\nDuring his interim tenure, Neuvivo completed a retrospective analysis of two Phase 2 studies that transformed the company's development strategy. ----------------------------------------------